 "convention": {
  "pink": "",
  "green": "Comments / explanations / indication of further work: non-binding and non-regulatory ARTICLE F1: GENERAL PRINCIPLES 3 ARTICLE F2: SCOPE, SANCTIONS AND BREACHES 4 ARTICLE F3: COMPETITORS’ SHUTDOWN PERIOD 5 F3.1 F1 Team Factory Shutdown Periods 5 F3.2 Power Unit Manufacturer Factory Shutdown Periods 6 F3.2.1 All PU Manufacturers must observe two shutdown periods: 6 ARTICLE F4: AERODYNAMIC TESTING RESTRICTIONS (ATR) 8 F4.1 General conditions 8 F4.2 Restricted Wind Tunnel Testing (RWTT) 9 F4.3 RWTT Permitted technology 10 F4.4 Restricted CFD (RCFD) simulations 12 F4.5 Exceptions to the Aerodynamic Testing Restrictions (ATR) 15 F4.6 Limits, Reporting, Inspection and Audit 16 F4.7 Movement of Personnel 18 ARTICLE F5: POWER UNIT TEST BENCH RESTRICTIONS 19 F5.1 Power Units Test Benches 19 F5.2 Power Unit Test Benches Operational Restrictions 23 F5.3 Power Unit Test Bench activities affecting PU Manufacturers and F1 Teams 26 APPENDIX F1: DEFINITIONS 30 PART A: GENERAL DEFINITIONS 30 PART B: DEFINITIONS APPROVED UNDER THE PROVISIONS OF THE PU GOVERNANCE AGREEMENT 30 APPENDIX F2: APPROVED CHANGES TO SECTION F FOR SUBSEQUENT YEARS 31 Changes for 2027 31 Changes for 2028 31 Changes for 2029 31",
  "red": "a. The first period of fourteen (14) consecutive calendar days during the months of July and/or August. If two consecutive Events during this period are separated by only seventeen (17) days a shutdown period of thirteen (13) consecutive calendar days must be observed. b. The second period, only from 2023, of nine (9) consecutive calendar days starting on the 24 December. Power Units for the 2022-2025 Championships must be concurrent between the two Power Unit programmes (2022-2025, and 2026-2030). and/or unions impose a different closing week, these factories may replace one week out of two weeks of the shutdown period specified in Article F3.1.1a. by the locally imposed week and have their second shutdown period specified in Article F3.1.1b. starting no later than 31 December. PU Manufacturers affected by this must make a declaration to the FIA that the staff concerned will not be permitted to transfer to work in the country that isn’t shutdown during these periods. thirty (30) days of the start of the Championship of that year. instruct a third-party supplier to carry out any of the following activities for or on behalf of the PU Manufacturer: a. Any work activity by any employee, consultant or sub-contractor engaged in design, development or production (excluding any work activity to be undertaken at the circuit in preparation for the Event immediately following the shutdown periods)."
 },
